h the biggest  challenges they're facing in their  companies right now right talk to those  people really get to know them and  they'll tell you they may not tell you  the solution you have to come up with  that but they'll tell you their problems  they'll tell you their pain and if  somebody is telling you a big pain  there's an opportunity to potentially  solve it  so let me give you two examples from my  own experience okay  I sell the entrepreneurs and I sell two  brands when it's telling entrepreneurs  it may be content like this video it may  be the Zuka guys I'm selling it may be a  workshop whatever it is I can understand  entrepreneurs I know what content to  create because I'm an entrepreneur right  this is the stuff I wish I had I had to  struggle through this crap I've started  my own business and failing and wanting  to quit and then eventually building it  up and turn it around and being acquired  and all of that stuff so I'll share my  lessons I know what I would have wanted  and I wish this stuff was there for me  when I was getting started so I am my  own audience the second part is I sell  the brands now I'm not I'm not a brand  right I'm not a huge company I'm not  Microsoft I'm not Dell I'm not Google  but I sell to those guys but I can speak  their language I got close to them  we have lunches and dinners and coffees  and sessions together right I help them  plan and so I know the problems that  they're going through by getting close  to them if you are not your target  customer and you're not close to your  target customer then how you're going to  find their major problem and find a  product that will help solve it so  that's my advice the best one is if you  are your own customer and you love it  because other people you know there are  other people out there who are just like  you who want it too but if you can't if  you're not your customer then hanging  around your customers and get really  close to them believe that's my advice I  love to